{"content":[{"c":["AHITUB"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Member of the priestly line of Aaron’s youngest son, Ithamar. Ahitub was a descendant of Eli through Eli’s son Phinehas and father of Ahijah and Ahimelech, who were priests during Saul’s reign (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.14.3","r":"1Sam.14.3","rawR":"1Sam.14.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.14.3","value":"1Sam.14.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 14:3"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.22.9-12,20","r":"1Sam.22.9-12,20","rawR":"1Sam.22.9-12,20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.22.9-12,20","value":"1Sam.22.9-12,20"}],"t":"ref","v":"22:9-12, 20"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Member of the priestly line of Aaron’s third son, Eleazar. Ahitub was Meraioth’s grandson, Amariah’s son, and father of Zadok (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.4-7","r":"1Chr.6.4-7","rawR":"1Chr.6.4-7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.4-7","value":"1Chr.6.4-7"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 6:4-7"},"). Zadok was a chief priest during David’s reign (",{"href":"?bref=2Sam.8.17","r":"2Sam.8.17","rawR":"2Sam.8.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Sam.8.17","value":"2Sam.8.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Sm 8:17"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Possibly the same as #2 above (the scribes sometimes mistakenly copied names twice), but more likely another member of the priestly line of Eleazar, seven generations after #2 (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.11-12","r":"1Chr.6.11-12","rawR":"1Chr.6.11-12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.11-12","value":"1Chr.6.11-12"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 6:11-12"},"). This Ahitub’s father was also named Amariah and his son or grandson Zadok (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.9.11","r":"1Chr.9.11","rawR":"1Chr.9.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.9.11","value":"1Chr.9.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 9:11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.11.11","r":"Neh.11.11","rawR":"Neh.11.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.11.11","value":"Neh.11.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 11:11"},"), but his grandfather was Azariah. Ahitub is listed as an ancestor of Ezra (",{"href":"?bref=Ezra.7.2","r":"Ezra.7.2","rawR":"Ezra.7.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezra.7.2","value":"Ezra.7.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ezr 7:2"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Esd.8.2","r":"1Esd.8.2","rawR":"1Esd.8.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Esd.8.2","value":"1Esd.8.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Esd 8:2"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=2Esd.1.1","r":"2Esd.1.1","rawR":"2Esd.1.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Esd.1.1","value":"2Esd.1.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Esd 1:1"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Ahitub","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Sm 14:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.14.3","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.14.3","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.14.3"},{"anchorText":"22:9-12, 20","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.22.9-12,20","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.22.9-12,20","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.22.9-12,20"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 6:4-7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.6.4-7","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.6.4-7","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.6.4-7"},{"anchorText":"2 Sm 8:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Sam.8.17","rawQueryValue":"2Sam.8.17","sourceRefExact":"2Sam.8.17"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 6:11-12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.6.11-12","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.6.11-12","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.6.11-12"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 9:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.9.11","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.9.11","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.9.11"},{"anchorText":"Neh 11:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.11.11","rawQueryValue":"Neh.11.11","sourceRefExact":"Neh.11.11"},{"anchorText":"Ezr 7:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezra.7.2","rawQueryValue":"Ezra.7.2","sourceRefExact":"Ezra.7.2"},{"anchorText":"1 Esd 8:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Esd.8.2","rawQueryValue":"1Esd.8.2","sourceRefExact":"1Esd.8.2"},{"anchorText":"2 Esd 1:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Esd.1.1","rawQueryValue":"2Esd.1.1","sourceRefExact":"2Esd.1.1"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"64e2fe13447ea4fbe4c5a06a7bd7599f2383365ce00a5a468e194f36eb406667","sourceItemName":"Ahitub","sourceItemOrder":201,"sourceMember":"Articles/A.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Ahitub","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Ahitub","title":"Ahitub","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}